# No Config Access Wrapper Classes

Do **not** add static helper classes whose only job is loading a config asset (`*Access`, `*Source`, `*Provider`, `*Loader`).

`ResourceManager` already holds registered assets for the session. Call `ResourceManager.Load<T>(address)` at the use site, or keep a **reference field** on the owning type and read fields from that ScriptableObject at runtime — so Inspector edits apply without re-init.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — needless indirection
static class GameplayConfigAccess
{
    static GameplayConfig _config;
    public static GameplayConfig Get() { ... }
}

// ❌ BAD — copies SO fields; Inspector changes won't apply until re-init
private void Initialize(GameplayConfig config)
{
    _dragStartPixels = config.dragStartPixels;
}

// ✅ GOOD — load where needed
_gameplayConfig = ResourceManager.Load<GameplayConfig>(GameplayConfig.Address);

// ✅ GOOD — hold the SO reference; read live fields
public bool DragInputEnabled => _gameplayConfig.dragInputEnabled;
```

## Allowed

- `[SerializeField] private GameplayConfig _config` on a MonoBehaviour, wired in the scene/prefab.
- An instance field holding the loaded SO on the type that owns the config for the session.
- **Logic** helpers that take an already-loaded config as a parameter — not loaders.

## Not allowed

- New static singleton/accessor classes wrapping `ResourceManager.Load` for configs.
- Copying config SO fields into private primitives/bools on init when live reads are intended.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No new `*Access` / `*Source` / `*Provider` / `*Loader` config classes
- [ ] Config loaded with `ResourceManager.Load<T>` or a serialized reference
- [ ] Runtime reads go through the SO reference, not stale field copies
